## Why This Is Asked
Designing adaptive models under load tests real-time orchestration and governance in GCP. It probes latency budgeting, feature-store usage, and rollback mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-model online/offline design
- Vertex AI Endpoints traffic splitting
- Real-time feature engineering with Pub/Sub/Dataflow/Feature Store
- Drift and latency monitoring, rollback via registry pinning
- Data Catalog lineage for auditability

## Code Example
```javascript
function chooseModel(latency, budget){
  if (latency <= 100 && budget > 0){
    return 'lightweight';
  }
  return 'heavy';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a compliant, scalable multi-tenant ML workflow on GCP with governance, explainability, and safety nets.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-aware Vertex AI deployment (endpoints/regions)
- Per-tenant Feature Stores and Model Registry
- Data residency and lineage via Data Catalog
- Explainable AI and per-tenant fairness checks
- Drift detection and safe rollback via canaries
- Monitoring/alerts with Cloud Monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift monitor for a tenant
function monitorDrift(tenant, current, baseline){
  const p = ksTest(current, baseline);
  if(p < 0.05){
    triggerRollback(tenant);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant drift detectors in staging?
- How do you ensure no data leakage across tenants while sharing infra?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design privacy-preserving cross-tenant ML pipelines with real-time inference, deployment discipline, and enterprise-grade governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation and differential privacy for cross-tenant insights
- Per-tenant feature stores with isolated data domains
- Vertex AI canary deployments with traffic splitting
- Real-time endpoints with autoscaling and cost budget controls
- Data lineage tracking in Data Catalog
- Drift monitoring (CTR) and latency SLAs logged to BigQuery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vertex AI Canary Rollout Configuration
const canaryDeployment = {
  endpoint: {
    displayName: 'ad-click-prediction-endpoint',
    model: 'ad-click-model-v1',
    trafficSplit: { '0': 20, '1': 80 } // 20% canary, 80% production
  },
  monitoring: {
    driftThresholds: { ctr: 0.05 },
    latencyThresholds: { p99: 200 },
    alertBudgetPercent: 80
  }
};
```
